#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203803 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204008 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0afa4d8-6d02-52c6-9836-12089de8f406" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Sums of Squares Given a Dataset or Summary Statistics"}] :question/id #uuid "6f0e3d4b-943b-5710-a996-ac4d3c68778d" :question/math-academy-id "e-16399" :question/problem "Consider the two sets of $5$ paired observations shown in the table below.\n\n| **$\\, x_i \\,$** | $15$ | $12$ | $13$ | $16$ | $19$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$\\, y_i \\,$** | $8$ | $13$ | $6$ | $15$ | $13$ |\n\nCalculate $S_{xy}.$" :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations $x_{1}, x_2, \\ldots, x_{n}$ and $y_{1}, y_2, \\ldots, y_{n},$ $S_{xy}$ is the sum of products of the deviations of $x_i$ and $y_i$ from their respective means, that is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the sample means $\\overline{x}$ and $\\overline{y}{:}$\n\n$$\n\\overline{x} = \\dfrac{15+12+13+16+19}{5} = 15\n$$\n\n$$\n\\overline{y} = \\dfrac{8+13+6+15+13}{5} = 11\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the differences between the $x_i$ and $\\overline{x}$, $y_i$ and $\\overline{y}$, and their product.\n\n| **$\\, x_i \\,$** | $15$ | $12$ | $13$ | $16$ | $19$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$\\, y_i \\,$** | $8$ | $13$ | $6$ | $15$ | $13$ |\n| **$\\, (x_i - \\overline{x}) \\,$** | $0$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $1$ | $4$ |\n| **$\\, (y_i - \\overline{y}) \\,$** | $-3$ | $2$ | $-5$ | $4$ | $2$ |\n| **$\\, (x_i - \\overline{x})(y_i - \\overline{y}) \\,$** | $0$ | $-6$ | $10$ | $4$ | $8$ |\n\nTherefore, $S_{xy}$ is\n\n$$\nS_{xy} = 0 + (-6) + 10 + 4 + 8 = 16.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203804 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204011 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "83df73fc-c0cc-5605-9b39-453de0c37cc7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating S(x,y) Using the Shortcut Formula"}] :question/id #uuid "489e5ffd-9e78-567b-b009-25d0c004825a" :question/math-academy-id "e-16400" :question/problem "Consider two sets of $30$ paired observations $x_{1}, x_2, \\ldots, x_{30},$ and $y_{1}, y_2, \\ldots, y_{30}.$ You are given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\sum }_{i=1}^{30}{x}_{i}=315, \\\\  & {\\sum }_{i=1}^{30}{y}_{i}=278, \\\\  & {\\sum }_{i=1}^{30}{x}_{i}{y}_{i}=2\\,964.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDetermine $S_{xy}.$" :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations $x_{1}, x_2, \\ldots, x_{n}$ and $y_{1}, y_2, \\ldots, y_{n},$ the statistic $S_{xy}$ can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}{y}_{i}-\\frac{1}{n}({\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i})({\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given statistics in the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & =2\\,964-\\frac{1}{30}(315)(278) \\\\  & =2\\,964-2\\,919 \\\\  & =45.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203805 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204009 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "714000f9-caea-57a3-a8cb-6b8ec99960d1" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Variance and Covariance"}] :question/id #uuid "7daa2313-4672-5624-aac2-e3b87b6ec366" :question/math-academy-id "e-16401" :question/problem "Consider two sets of $35$ paired observations $x_{1}, x_2, \\ldots, x_{35},$ and $y_{1}, y_2, \\ldots, y_{35}.$ You are given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx}=35,\\,{S}_{yy}=133,\\,{S}_{xy}=105.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of $\\mathrm{Cov}(x, y)?$" :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations $x_{1}, x_2, \\ldots, x_{n}$ and $y_{1}, y_2, \\ldots, y_{n},$ their covariance can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Cov(x,y) & =\\frac{{S}_{xy}}{n},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $S_{xy}$ is the sum of products of the deviations of $x_i$ and $y_i$ from their means.\n\nWe are given that $S_{xy} = 105.$ Substituting the given statistic in the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Cov(x,y) & =\\frac{105}{35} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203806 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204010 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1f0ed04b-f011-5818-952d-425a19e0cd5c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Sums of Squares Using the Shortcut Formula"}] :question/id #uuid "9804df95-f494-5d99-acbd-97c69344d401" :question/math-academy-id "e-16402" :question/problem "Consider the two sets of $5$ paired observations shown in the table below.\n\n| **$\\, x_i \\,$** | $10$ | $9$ | $8$ | $8$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$\\, y_i \\,$** | $15$ | $12$ | $14$ | $12$ | $8$ |\n\nGiven that $\\displaystyle\\sum_{i=1}^5 x_i^2 = 334,$ calculate $S_{xx}.$" :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations $x_{1}, x_2, \\ldots, x_{n}$ and $y_{1}, y_2, \\ldots, y_{n},$ the sum of squared deviations from the mean for the data $x_i$ can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2}-\\frac{1}{n}{({\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the sum of the $x_i$ data:\n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^n x_i = 10 + 9 + 8 + 8 + 5 = 40.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\displaystyle\\sum_{i=1}^5 x_i^2 = 334.$\n\nFinally, by substituting into the above formula, we get\n\n$$\nS_{xx} =334 - \\dfrac{1}{5}(40)^2 = 334- 320 = 14.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204446 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204011 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "83df73fc-c0cc-5605-9b39-453de0c37cc7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating S(x,y) Using the Shortcut Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44123af5-e2fd-5ea4-88e9-b70e9b3b267f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=85.7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512240} {:answer/id #uuid "b32a8445-2ca4-5860-9a66-a3720ee75b12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=41.9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512522} {:answer/id #uuid "b564aa2d-1815-5b26-8895-65a367b53773" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512529} {:answer/id #uuid "f38077d2-538a-52de-80fc-f81b787769d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512689} {:answer/id #uuid "ffef375f-eee1-5328-8ca8-8a877b28f600" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512721}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ffef375f-eee1-5328-8ca8-8a877b28f600" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512721} :answer-field/id #uuid "880bbb07-a5bf-59b4-b7df-bceda5d80f95" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186202607}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3afcb82f-1e68-5666-b8c9-5cc1b12c399d" :question/math-academy-id "q-251493" :question/problem "Consider the two sets of $6$ paired observations shown in the table below.\n\n| **$\\,{x}_{i}\\,$** | $2$ | $3$ | $9$ | $7$ | $5$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$\\,{y}_{i}\\,$** | $16$ | $15$ | $14$ | $23$ | $18$ | $15$ |\n\nGiven that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{6}{x}_{i}{y}_{i}=514,$ calculate ${S}_{xy}.$" :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ the sum of products of deviations from the means can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i}{x}_{i}{y}_{i}-\\frac{1}{n}({\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i})({\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the sum of the ${x}_{i}$ and ${y}_{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} & =2+3+9+7+5+4=30, \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i} & =16+15+14+23+18+15=101\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe are given that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{6}{x}_{i}{y}_{i}=514.$\n\nFinally, substituting in the above formula we get\n\n$$\n{S}_{xy}=514-\\frac{1}{6}(30)(101)=514-505=9.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204448 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204009 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "714000f9-caea-57a3-a8cb-6b8ec99960d1" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Variance and Covariance"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "453923a5-93c8-5c6f-bfec-b6cdf2b78c6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.56" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536389}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "453923a5-93c8-5c6f-bfec-b6cdf2b78c6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.56" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536389} :answer-field/id #uuid "813072e4-450e-5ca8-9448-486d80a9833f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186202614}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f5f36809-3c9f-5a12-9f4a-44402dbf641c" :question/math-academy-id "q-251495" :question/problem "Consider two sets of $25$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{25},$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{25}.$ You are given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx}=125,\\,{S}_{yy}=37,\\,{S}_{xy}=64.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, $Cov(x,y)=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ their covariance can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Cov(x,y) & =\\frac{{S}_{xy}}{n},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${S}_{xy}$ is the sum of products of the deviations of ${x}_{i}$ and ${y}_{i}$ from their means.\n\nWe are given that ${S}_{xy}=64.$ Substituting the given statistic in the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Cov(x,y) & =\\frac{64}{25} \\\\  & =2.56.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233680 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204011 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "83df73fc-c0cc-5605-9b39-453de0c37cc7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating S(x,y) Using the Shortcut Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2032787c-d22e-592f-81df-10f4faf70894" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536330} {:answer/id #uuid "38df4399-89bc-529e-b1a6-df9d281a088f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536373} {:answer/id #uuid "6586d857-9cd0-591a-a6b4-187ac642b6a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=36.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536458} {:answer/id #uuid "9050f4d8-8c17-564c-9e1c-31ba36d7157b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536514} {:answer/id #uuid "cfd589a9-8236-5537-bc1d-3196c955ccaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=32.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536612}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2032787c-d22e-592f-81df-10f4faf70894" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536330} :answer-field/id #uuid "b96494db-5dd2-5488-8cf6-d406dbf495a4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536779}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e13cfbef-51cd-58dd-b88f-cef6834b30f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-251801" :question/problem "Consider the two sets of $6$ paired observations in the table below.\n\n| **$\\,{x}_{i}\\,$** | $1$ | $7$ | $3$ | $4$ | $6$ | $10$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$\\,{y}_{i}\\,$** | $11$ | $3$ | $7$ | $2$ | $1$ | $18$ |\n\nGiven that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{6}{x}_{i}{y}_{i}=247,$ calculate ${S}_{xy}.$" :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ the sum of products of deviations from the means can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i}{x}_{i}{y}_{i}-\\frac{1}{n}({\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i})({\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the sum of the ${x}_{i}$ and ${y}_{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} & =1+7+3+4+6+10=31, \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i} & =11+3+7+2+1+18=42\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe are given that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{6}{x}_{i}{y}_{i}=247.$\n\nFinally, by substituting in the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n{S}_{xy}=247-\\frac{1}{6}(31)(42)=247-217=30.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536838 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204010 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1f0ed04b-f011-5818-952d-425a19e0cd5c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Sums of Squares Using the Shortcut Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e22bc458-30f2-56c5-a752-2720115543c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1250" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536636}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e22bc458-30f2-56c5-a752-2720115543c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1250" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536636} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ae99c74-d6dc-56f1-8e0e-a0b4df319323" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536704}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5cbb4944-93ba-5c18-a003-1720623144e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-251837" :question/problem "Consider two sets of $27$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{27},$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{27}.$ You are given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\sum }_{i=1}^{27}{x}_{i}=540,\\,{\\sum }_{i=1}^{27}{y}_{i}=567, \\\\  & {\\sum }_{i=1}^{27}{x}_{i}^{2}=12\\,050,\\,{\\sum }_{i=1}^{27}{y}_{i}^{2}=14\\,107.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the sum of the squared deviations from the mean for the points ${x}_{i}.$\n\n${S}_{xx}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ the sum of squared deviations from the mean for the data ${x}_{i}$ can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2}-\\frac{1}{n}{({\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i})}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given statistics in the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx} & =12\\,050-\\frac{1}{27}(540)^{2} \\\\  & =12\\,050-10\\,800 \\\\  & =1\\,250.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186521455 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204009 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "714000f9-caea-57a3-a8cb-6b8ec99960d1" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Variance and Covariance"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e38fe49d-81c4-5be4-8d42-66e01917801d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521274}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e38fe49d-81c4-5be4-8d42-66e01917801d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521274} :answer-field/id #uuid "f25616a1-e3e9-5a57-bef3-4345308333c4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521449}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "094cdd1f-e814-5164-bdf6-dc0f3e0f507e" :question/math-academy-id "q-251857" :question/problem "Consider two sets of $40$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{40},$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{40}.$ You are given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx}=54,\\,{S}_{yy}=35,\\,{S}_{xy}=188.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, $Cov(x,y)=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ their covariance can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Cov(x,y) & =\\frac{{S}_{xy}}{n},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${S}_{xy}$ is the sum of products of the deviations of ${x}_{i}$ and ${y}_{i}$ from their means.\n\nWe are given that ${S}_{xy}=188.$ Substituting the given statistic in the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Cov(x,y) & =\\frac{188}{40} \\\\  & =4.7.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536828 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204008 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0afa4d8-6d02-52c6-9836-12089de8f406" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Sums of Squares Given a Dataset or Summary Statistics"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47de3422-ffeb-5a17-b14f-74498ea093ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=7.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536393} {:answer/id #uuid "7d408cf0-77ba-54f6-afce-3f39ab3ef960" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=9.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536490} {:answer/id #uuid "d3e6e201-f276-5cd8-881c-e11c2c1e59c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=9.0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536617} {:answer/id #uuid "ee5147e7-4d0d-55e3-9a32-5af3e4b874b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=6.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536663} {:answer/id #uuid "f1f5c552-e8d5-558d-8758-dda8b1d41492" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=7.9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536669}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47de3422-ffeb-5a17-b14f-74498ea093ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=7.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536393} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d05e707-cf16-5915-a547-c70d2c206fee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536763}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3b535844-eddd-540b-a454-365555c2e28f" :question/math-academy-id "q-251875" :question/problem "Consider the two sets of $5$ paired observations shown in the table below.\n\n| **$\\,{x}_{i}\\,$** | $5$ | $8$ | $9$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$\\,{y}_{i}\\,$** | $8$ | $9$ | $10$ | $7$ | $9$ |\n\nCalculate ${S}_{xy}.$" :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ ${S}_{xy}$ is the sum of products of the deviations of ${x}_{i}$ and ${y}_{i}$ from their respective means, that is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the sample means $\\overset{―}{x}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}:$\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{5+8+9+5+6}{5}=6.6\n$$\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{8+9+10+7+9}{5}=8.6\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the differences between the ${x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{x}$, ${y}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}$, and their product.\n\n| **$\\,{x}_{i}\\,$** | $5$ | $8$ | $9$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$\\,{y}_{i}\\,$** | $8$ | $9$ | $10$ | $7$ | $9$ |\n| **$\\,({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})\\,$** | $-1.6$ | $1.4$ | $2.4$ | $-1.6$ | $-0.6$ |\n| **$\\,({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y})\\,$** | $-0.6$ | $0.4$ | $1.4$ | $-1.6$ | $0.4$ |\n| **$\\,({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y})\\,$** | $0.96$ | $0.56$ | $3.36$ | $2.56$ | $-0.24$ |\n\nTherefore, ${S}_{xy}$ is\n\n$$\n{S}_{xy}=0.96+0.56+3.36+2.56+(-0.24)=7.2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536892 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204008 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0afa4d8-6d02-52c6-9836-12089de8f406" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Sums of Squares Given a Dataset or Summary Statistics"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f654eb5-da33-51e7-b9e3-237f2b57649d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=2.80" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536328} {:answer/id #uuid "3a4e3e32-81eb-5215-b6e7-ca840cc59c2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=0.06" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536374} {:answer/id #uuid "87b37972-f264-5fe7-be91-6532a22909a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=0.14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536504} {:answer/id #uuid "e2058f1c-ca6b-5704-b24a-ad1af833dee9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=1.33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536634} {:answer/id #uuid "f0f966f8-f580-5c9c-9ccf-b3a48389f82a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=1.12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536665}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87b37972-f264-5fe7-be91-6532a22909a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=0.14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536504} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b37bc23-4463-5cf2-acb2-e2f4162f0ffc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536738}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e546cbd8-6c28-59cf-9108-41c070e316fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-251876" :question/problem "Consider the two sets of $7$ paired observations shown in the table below.\n\n| **$\\,{x}_{i}\\,$** | $1.2$ | $1.0$ | $0.7$ | $1.3$ | $1.8$ | $1.7$ | $1.4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$\\,{y}_{i}\\,$** | $6.6$ | $6.1$ | $5.7$ | $6.0$ | $6.3$ | $5.9$ | $5.4$ |\n\nCalculate ${S}_{xy}.$" :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ ${S}_{xy}$ is the sum of products of the deviations of ${x}_{i}$ and ${y}_{i}$ from their respective means, that is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the sample means $\\overset{―}{x}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}:$\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1.2+1.0+0.7+1.3+1.8+1.4+1.7}{7}=1.3\n$$\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{6.6+6.1+5.7+6.0+6.3+5.9+5.4}{7}=6\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the differences between the ${x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{x}$, ${y}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}$, and their product.\n\n| **$\\,{x}_{i}\\,$** | $1.2$ | $1.0$ | $0.7$ | $1.3$ | $1.8$ | $1.7$ | $1.4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$\\,{y}_{i}\\,$** | $6.6$ | $6.1$ | $5.7$ | $6.0$ | $6.3$ | $5.9$ | $5.4$ |\n| **$\\,({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})\\,$** | $-0.1$ | $-0.3$ | $-0.6$ | $0$ | $0.5$ | $0.4$ | $0.1$ |\n| **$\\,({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y})\\,$** | $0.6$ | $0.1$ | $-0.3$ | $0$ | $0.3$ | $-0.1$ | $-0.6$ |\n| **$\\,({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y})\\,$** | $-0.06$ | $-0.03$ | $0.18$ | $0$ | $0.15$ | $-0.04$ | $-0.06$ |\n\nTherefore, ${S}_{xy}$ is\n\n$$\n{S}_{xy}=(-0.06)+(-0.03)+0.18+0+0.15+(-0.04)+(-0.06)=0.14.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512955 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204010 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1f0ed04b-f011-5818-952d-425a19e0cd5c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Sums of Squares Using the Shortcut Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a2dd6fd3-36d2-5d1e-bf27-1912d3b0ed19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "590" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512478}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a2dd6fd3-36d2-5d1e-bf27-1912d3b0ed19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "590" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512478} :answer-field/id #uuid "101037bb-1cdc-5f57-adda-e1f24aa1b97f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512734}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f69f9435-629a-5550-ae7c-8e46c05363dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-251891" :question/problem "Consider two sets of $20$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{20},$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{20}.$ You are given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\sum }_{i=1}^{20}{x}_{i}=400,\\,{\\sum }_{i=1}^{20}{y}_{i}=440, \\\\  & {\\sum }_{i=1}^{20}{x}_{i}^{2}=8\\,590,\\,{\\sum }_{i=1}^{20}{y}_{i}^{2}=9\\,740.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the sum of the squared deviations from the mean for the points ${x}_{i}.$\n\n${S}_{xx}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ the sum of squared deviations from the mean for the data ${x}_{i}$ can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2}-\\frac{1}{n}{({\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i})}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given statistics in the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx} & =8\\,590-\\frac{1}{20}(400)^{2} \\\\  & =8\\,590-8\\,000 \\\\  & =590.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
